.tp-card{background:rgba(20,20,23,.72);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:12px}
.tp-card b{display:block;color:var(--cream);font-size:12px;margin-bottom:5px}
.tp-card span{color:var(--txt2);font-size:12px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.55}
.pdp-help-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:10px;margin:16px 0}
.pdp-help{min-height:46px;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--line2);background:rgba(255,255,255,.045);color:var(--cream);font-weight:900;font-family:inherit;text-decoration:none;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:6px;padding:10px;transition:var(--tr)}
.pdp-help:hover{border-color:var(--gold-br);color:var(--gold2)}
.acc{border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
.acc summary{cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;padding:17px 2px;font-weight:800;font-size:15px;color:var(--cream)}
.acc summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
.acc summary::after{content:"+";font-family:var(--lt);color:var(--gold);font-size:20px;transition:transform .25s}
.acc[open] summary::after{content:"−"}
.acc-body{padding:0 2px 18px;color:var(--txt2);font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.9}
/* ═══ product description + category links (added 2026-08-05) ═══
   Class is .pdp-body, NOT .pdp-desc — .pdp-desc already exists in this template
   for the short auto-generated summary paragraph that also feeds the Product
   schema `description`. Reusing that name double-styled both blocks and made
   `document.querySelector('.pdp-desc')` ambiguous.

   Deliberately reuses the same tokens as .acc-body above. Those render
   correctly on this template today, so matching them avoids the token
   inversion trap (lbass-stamp redefines --cream/--ink2/--gold globally). */
.pdp-body{margin:22px 0 0;color:var(--txt2);font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.9}
.pdp-body p{margin:0 0 12px}
.pdp-body ul{margin:10px 0 14px;padding-inline-start:20px}
.pdp-body li{margin:3px 0;color:var(--txt2)}
.pdp-body strong,.pdp-body b{color:var(--cream)}
.pdp-body a{color:var(--gold2);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}
.pdp-body h2{font-size:16px;margin:20px 0 10px;color:var(--cream);font-weight:800}
.pdp-body details{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:11px 0}
.pdp-body details summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:800;color:var(--cream);font-size:14.5px;
  list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:10px}
.pdp-body details summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
.pdp-body details summary::after{content:'+';color:var(--gold2);font-weight:900;flex:none}
.pdp-body details[open] summary::after{content:'−'}
.pdp-body details p{margin:9px 0 2px;font-size:14px}
.pdp-cats{margin:24px 0 0;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
.pdp-cats-h{margin:0 0 9px;font-size:13px;font-weight:800;color:var(--txt3)}
.pdp-cats a{display:inline-block;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:30px;
  padding:7px 14px;margin:0 6px 7px 0;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:var(--txt2);
  transition:border-color .2s ease,color .2s ease}
.pdp-cats a:hover{border-color:var(--gold2);color:var(--cream)}
/* ═══ PRODUCT LIGHTBOX — rebuilt 2026-08-10 ═══
   THE DISTORTION BUG: the old markup was
       <img id="zoomImg" ... width="1200" height="1500">
   Those intrinsic attributes give the element an implicit aspect-ratio of 4:5.
   Combined with max-width/max-height percentages and no object-fit, EVERY photo
   was letterboxed into a 4:5 box and stretched to fill it, whatever its real
   dimensions. The fix is structural: no width/height attributes on the modal
   image at all, plus object-fit:contain. Never re-add them here — they are
   correct on the inline gallery img (fixed-size container) and wrong here.

   Z-INDEX: the old value was 120, which LOST to snippets/lbass-menu.liquid (200)
   and templates/index.liquid (300), and merely tied with the cart drawer (120).
   That is why the header/menu/cart could sit on top of the modal. */
.zoomlb{position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:99999;background:rgba(5,5,6,.96);display:none;align-items:center;justify-content:center;overscroll-behavior:contain;-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent}
.zoomlb.show{display:flex}
.zoomlb__stage{margin:0;padding:0;width:100%;height:100%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}
.zoomlb__img{width:auto;height:auto;max-width:100vw;max-height:90vh;object-fit:contain;display:block;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;-webkit-user-drag:none}
.zoomlb .x{position:absolute;top:14px;right:14px;z-index:2;width:48px;height:48px;border-radius:50%;border:1px solid rgba(244,239,230,.34);color:#F4EFE6;font-size:20px;line-height:1;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:rgba(10,10,11,.72);cursor:pointer;backdrop-filter:blur(10px);touch-action:manipulation}
.zoomlb .x:hover,.zoomlb .x:focus-visible{background:rgba(10,10,11,.95);border-color:rgba(244,239,230,.7)}
.zoomlb__nav{position:absolute;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);z-index:2;width:52px;height:52px;border-radius:50%;border:1px solid rgba(244,239,230,.3);background:rgba(10,10,11,.68);color:#F4EFE6;font-size:26px;line-height:1;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;cursor:pointer;backdrop-filter:blur(10px);touch-action:manipulation;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:isolate;padding-bottom:3px}
.zoomlb__nav:hover,.zoomlb__nav:focus-visible{background:rgba(10,10,11,.95);border-color:rgba(244,239,230,.7)}
.zoomlb__nav[hidden]{display:none}
.zoomlb__nav--prev{left:14px}
.zoomlb__nav--next{right:14px}
.zoomlb__count{position:absolute;bottom:18px;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);z-index:2;margin:0;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:999px;background:rgba(10,10,11,.72);border:1px solid rgba(244,239,230,.22);color:#F4EFE6;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.04em;direction:ltr;backdrop-filter:blur(10px)}
.zoomlb__count[hidden]{display:none}
@media(max-width:767px){
  .zoomlb__img{max-height:86vh}
  .zoomlb__nav{width:44px;height:44px;font-size:22px}
  .zoomlb__nav--prev{left:6px}
  .zoomlb__nav--next{right:6px}
  .zoomlb .x{top:10px;right:10px;width:44px;height:44px}
  .zoomlb__count{bottom:12px}
}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.zoomlb,.zoomlb *{transition:none!important;animation:none!important}}
.pdp-sticky{position:fixed;bottom:0;inset-inline:0;z-index:98;display:none;gap:9px;align-items:center;padding:10px 12px calc(10px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));background:rgba(10,10,11,.96);border-top:1px solid var(--line);transition:transform .35s cubic-bezier(.7,0,.3,1),visibility 0s linear 0s}
.pdp-sticky.tuck{transform:translateY(130%);visibility:hidden;pointer-events:none;transition:transform .35s cubic-bezier(.7,0,.3,1),visibility 0s linear .35s}
.pdp-sticky .info{flex:1;min-width:0}
.pdp-sticky .nm{font-weight:800;font-size:13px;color:var(--cream);white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;margin:0}
.pdp-sticky .cond{display:block;margin:2px 0 0;color:var(--gold2);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:900;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
.pdp-sticky .pr{font-family:var(--lt);font-weight:700;color:var(--gold);font-size:15px;direction:ltr;text-align:right;margin:0}
.pdp-sticky button,.pdp-sticky a{min-height:50px;padding:13px 17px;border-radius:var(--r-sm);font-weight:900;font-size:14px;flex-shrink:0;border:0;cursor:pointer;text-decoration:none;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}
.pdp-sticky button:disabled{opacity:.48;cursor:not-allowed}
.pdp-sticky-add{background:var(--cream);color:var(--ink)}
.pdp-sticky-wa{width:50px;padding:0!important;background:var(--green);color:#fff;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18)!important}
.pdp-sticky-wa svg{width:23px;height:23px;fill:currentColor}
.pdp-sticky button:focus-visible,.pdp-sticky a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--gold2);outline-offset:2px}
.pdp-emo-line{color:var(--gold2);font-style:italic;font-size:15px;font-weight:700;margin:-4px 0 12px;line-height:1.5}
.pdp-trio{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px;margin-bottom:18px}
.pdp-trio-card{background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(200,154,14,.08),rgba(255,255,255,.025));border:1px solid var(--gold-br);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px}
.ptc-h{font-size:12px;font-weight:900;color:var(--gold);margin:0 0 6px}
.ptc-b{font-size:13px;color:var(--txt);margin:0;line-height:1.6;font-weight:700}
.pdp-fits{margin-bottom:18px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px}
.pdp-fit-row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;padding:10px 14px;border-radius:var(--r-sm);font-size:13.5px;font-weight:700;color:var(--txt)}
.pdp-fit-yes{background:rgba(31,168,85,.08);border:1px solid rgba(31,168,85,.25)}
.pdp-fit-no{background:rgba(180,80,42,.08);border:1px solid rgba(180,80,42,.25)}
.pf-ic{font-size:16px;flex-shrink:0}
.pdp-fit-yes .pf-ic{color:var(--green)}
.pdp-fit-no .pf-ic{color:var(--clay2)}
.pdp-meas{margin-bottom:18px;padding:16px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--r-md);background:rgba(255,255,255,.025)}
.pm-h{font-weight:900;color:var(--cream);margin:0 0 4px}
.pm-sub{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--txt3);font-weight:700;margin:0 0 14px}
.pm-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(90px,1fr));gap:8px}
.pm-i{background:var(--ink2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:10px 8px;text-align:center}
.pm-i .k{display:block;font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;color:var(--txt3)}
.pm-i .v{display:block;font-family:var(--lt);font-size:15px;font-weight:700;color:var(--cream);direction:ltr;margin-top:2px}
.pm-note{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--txt3);font-weight:700;margin:12px 0 0}
.pdp-steps{margin-bottom:22px;padding:18px;border:1px solid var(--gold-br);border-radius:var(--r-md);background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(200,154,14,.06),transparent)}
.ps-h{font-weight:900;color:var(--gold2);margin:0 0 14px;font-size:15px}
.ps-list{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px}
.ps-list li{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px}
.ps-n{width:28px;height:28px;flex-shrink:0;border-radius:50%;background:var(--gold);color:var(--ink);font-family:var(--lt);font-weight:900;font-size:13px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}
.ps-t{font-size:14px;font-weight:700;color:var(--txt)}
@media(max-width:900px){
  .pdp-wrap{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding-bottom:170px}
  .pdp-gal{position:static}
  .pdp-buy-panel{position:relative;top:auto;padding:18px}
  .pdp-details-flow{margin-top:18px}
  .pdp-main-viz{height:clamp(360px,64vh,640px)}
  .pdp-nav{width:50px;height:50px}
  .pdp-nav::before{width:12px;height:12px;border-width:3px}
  .pdp-nav.prev{left:12px}
  .pdp-nav.next{right:12px}
  .pdp-sticky{display:flex}
  .tp-grid,.pdp-help-row,.pdp-trio{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .pdp-condition-card{grid-template-columns:1fr}
}
@media(max-width:420px){
  .pdp-sticky .info{max-width:108px}
  .pdp-sticky button{padding-inline:13px;font-size:13px}
}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
  .pdp-cart::after{display:none}
  .pdp-sticky{transition:none}
}
/* ════════════════ PDP PROOF BLOCK ════════════════ */
.pdp-proof{margin:24px 0 22px;padding:18px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--r-md);background:rgba(255,255,255,.025)}
.pdp-query-line{margin:-2px 0 14px;color:var(--cream);font-size:14px;font-weight:800;line-height:1.75}
.pdp-proof-h{font-size:15px;font-weight:900;color:var(--cream);margin-bottom:14px}
.pdp-proof-h em{font-style:normal;color:var(--gold2)}
.pdp-proof-list{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;display:grid;gap:10px}
.pp-row{display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font-size:13.5px}
.pp-row:last-child{border-bottom:0}
.pp-ic{font-family:var(--lt);font-weight:700;color:var(--gold2);min-width:32px;font-size:13.5px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;padding-top:1px}
.pp-row b{color:var(--cream);display:block;font-size:13.5px;margin-bottom:3px;font-weight:900}
.pp-row span{color:var(--txt2);line-height:1.65;font-weight:500}
.pp-row a{color:var(--green2);text-decoration:underline}
</style>

<div class="pdp-wrap">
  <nav class="pdp-crumb" aria-label="مسار التصفّح">
    <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">الرئيسية</a><span class="sep">›</span>
    {% if first_collection %}<a href="{{ first_collection.url }}">{{ first_collection.title }}</a><span class="sep">›</span>{% endif %}
    <span class="cur">{{ display_title }}</span>
  </nav>

  <div class="pdp-gal">
    <div class="pdp-main-viz" id="pdpMainViz" {% if main_image %}data-zoom="{{ main_image | image_url: width: 1600 }}" data-zoom-w="{{ main_image.width }}" data-zoom-h="{{ main_image.height }}" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="كبّر الصورة"{% endif %}>
      {% if main_image %}
        <img id="pdpMainImg" src="{{ main_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}" alt="{{ main_image.alt | default: product_image_alt | escape }}" fetchpriority="high" loading="eager" decoding="async" width="1200" height="1500">
        {% if product.images.size > 1 %}
          <button type="button" class="pdp-nav prev" data-pdp-prev aria-label="الصورة السابقة"></button>
          <button type="button" class="pdp-nav next" data-pdp-next aria-label="الصورة الموالية"></button>
          <span class="pdp-count" id="pdpImgCount" aria-live="polite">1 / {{ product.images.size }}</span>
        {% endif %}
      {% else %}
        <span style="font-size:120px;opacity:.35">{% case product.product_type %}{% when 'Jackets' %}🧥{% when 'Jeans' %}👖{% when 'T-Shirts' %}👕{% when 'Shoes' %}👟{% when 'Hoodies' %}🧣{% when 'Accessories' %}🕶{% when 'Pants' %}🧵{% else %}👕{% endcase %}</span>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% if product.images.size > 1 %}
      <div class="pdp-thumbs">
        {% for image in product.images %}
          <button type="button" class="pdp-thumb{% if forloop.first %} on{% endif %}" data-pdp-thumb data-index="{{ forloop.index0 }}" data-src="{{ image | image_url: width: 1200 }}" data-zoom="{{ image | image_url: width: 1600 }}" data-w="{{ image.width }}" data-h="{{ image.height }}" data-alt="{{ image.alt | default: product_image_alt | escape }}" aria-label="صورة {{ forloop.index }} من {{ product.images.size }}" aria-current="{% if forloop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}">
            <img src="{{ image | image_url: width: 200 }}" alt="" loading="lazy" width="200" height="250">
          </button>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    {% else %}
      <p class="pdp-gal-note">📷 بغيتي صور حقيقية إضافية ديال هاد القطعة بالضبط؟ <a href="https://wa.me/{{ wa_number }}?text={{ wa_msg_photos }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">سولنا فالواتساب</a></p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  <div class="pdp-info-col">
    <aside class="pdp-buy-panel" aria-label="معلومات الشراء">
    <p class="pdp-brand">{{ product.vendor }} — {% if is_new_condition %}NEW · REAL PHOTOS{% else %}SECOND-HAND · REAL PHOTOS{% endif %}</p>
    {%- comment -%}
      Product titles here are bilingual and pipe-separated, e.g.
        "Adidas Copa Black Football Boots - Size 44 | سبادري كورة أديداس"
      Rendering that as one H1 wraps badly and reads as truncated, because the
      browser applies the page's RTL direction to the whole string and the Latin
      half ends up visually out of order.

      Split on the pipe: the Latin half becomes the H1, the Arabic half becomes a
      support line beneath it. Both are real crawlable text, and the H1 stays a
      single element — no second H1 introduced.

      `dir="auto"` on each part lets the browser resolve direction from that
      part's own first strong character instead of inheriting RTL for both.

      Products WITHOUT a pipe render exactly as before: `ttl_ar` is blank, the
      support line is skipped, and the H1 is the full title.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign ttl_parts = display_title | split: ' | ' -%}
    {%- assign ttl_main = ttl_parts[0] | strip -%}
    {%- assign ttl_ar = '' -%}
    {%- if ttl_parts.size > 1 -%}{%- assign ttl_ar = ttl_parts[1] | strip -%}{%- endif -%}
    <h1 class="pdp-name" dir="auto">{% if query_h1 != blank %}{{ query_h1 }}{% else %}{{ ttl_main }}{% endif %}</h1>
    {% if query_answer != blank %}<p class="pdp-query-line">{{ query_answer }}</p>{% endif %}
    {%- if ttl_ar != blank -%}
      <p class="pdp-name-ar" dir="auto">{{ ttl_ar }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    <!-- Start of Judge.me code -->
    <div style='{{ jm_style }};margin:-6px 0 10px' class='jdgm-widget jdgm-preview-badge' data-id='{{ product.id }}' data-auto-install='false'>
      {{ product.metafields.judgeme.badge }}
    </div>
    <!-- End of Judge.me code -->
    {% if product.metafields.lbass.emo_line != blank %}
      <p class="pdp-emo-line">{{ product.metafields.lbass.emo_line }}</p>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="pdp-meta">
      {%- comment -%}
        DUPLICATE CONDITION PILL REMOVED 2026-08-23.
        This rendered {{ condition_label }} and so did the badges row 45px
        below it — the SAME string twice, in two different styles, because a
        later stylesheet redefines the gold tokens both rules use (--gold2 now
        resolves to #8F1F0D, a dark red). Measured on the live page:
            .pdp-grade            11.5px  cream on #0B0B0C
            .pdp-badge--condition 11.5px  #8F1F0D on a red tint
        One condition statement per page. The surviving one is in the badges
        row, where it sits beside "صور حقيقية" — the same grouping a collection
        card uses when it puts the condition chip next to the size chip.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="pdp-stock">
        {% if product.available %}
          {% if is_one_of_one %}⚡ قطعة وحدة فقط · 1/1{% else %}متوفرة دابا{% endif %}
        {% else %}
          هاد القطعة تباعت
        {% endif %}
      </span>
    </div>

    {% unless product.available %}
      {%- capture soldout_exclude_ids -%},{{ product.id }},{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- assign soldout_prefer_type = product.type | default: product.product_type -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        prefer_collection / prefer_vendor added 2026-08-29. Without them the rail
        drew from collections.all with no relevance filter, so this sold-out PDP
        — which holds 83 impressions for «بنطال تراك أسود للرجال» — was offering
        football boots and a crossbody bag while four in-stock black track pants
        sat in the same collection. Collection first, then vendor, then store-wide.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% render 'lbass-live-products-rail',
        heading: 'هاد القطعة تباعت — شوف البدائل',
        intro: 'قطع مشابهة ومتوفرة دابا قبل ما تكمل التصفح.',
        placement: 'sold_product_above_fold',
        limit: 2,
        exclude_ids: soldout_exclude_ids,
        prefer_type: soldout_prefer_type,
        prefer_collection: first_collection,
        prefer_vendor: product.vendor,
        compact: true
      %}
    {% endunless %}

    <div class="pdp-badges" aria-label="معلومات مختصرة">
      {%- comment -%}
        Uses its OWN class (.lb-cond) rather than .pdp-badge--condition. The
        badge classes in this file declare gold and render red, because a later
        tokens sheet redefines --gold2/--gold-dim/--gold-br. Rather than fight
        that cascade, this badge owns its colours outright so it looks the same
        wherever the sheet lands. Measured against the real ground: the PDP body
        computes to rgb(255,255,255), so these are dark-on-light.

        The "الحالة" label is the point of the change. Unlabelled, the pill just
        said «بحالة مزيانة بزاف» with nothing marking it as the condition grade —
        on a collection card the neighbouring size chip supplies that context,
        but on the product page it has to say so itself.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% if condition_confirmed %}<span class="lb-cond"><b>الحالة</b>{{ condition_label }}</span>{% endif %}
      {% if is_one_of_one %}<span class="pdp-badge lb-uniq" dir="auto">Pièce unique <i>· قطعة وحدة فقط</i></span>{% endif %}
      <span class="pdp-badge">صور حقيقية</span>
      {% if promo_visible %}<span class="pdp-badge pdp-badge--promo">{{ product.metafields.lbass.promo_badge.value | default: 'عرض على منتجات مختارة' }}</span>{% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="pdp-price-wrap">
      {%- comment -%}
        The discount sits ABOVE the price, on its own line, rather than trailing
        the row. Two reasons beyond "make it bigger":

          1. .pdp-prices is align-items:baseline. A badge large enough to be
             noticed cannot share a baseline with a clamp(22px,3vw,30px) price
             without one of them looking misaligned.
          2. On a phone that row wraps. A trailing badge is the element that
             wraps off, i.e. the promotion is what disappears first on the
             surface that matters most. On its own line it cannot.

        Same element, same data-savepct hook, so applySale() is untouched.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign pdp_pct = '' -%}
      {%- capture pdp_pct %}{% render 'lbass-sale', product: product, variant: product.selected_or_first_available_variant %}{% endcapture -%}
      {%- assign pdp_pct = pdp_pct | strip -%}
      {%- assign pdp_on_sale = false -%}
      {%- if product.selected_or_first_available_variant.compare_at_price and product.selected_or_first_available_variant.compare_at_price > product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price and pdp_pct != '0' -%}{%- assign pdp_on_sale = true -%}{%- endif -%}
      <p class="pdp-price-kicker">السعر الحالي</p>
      {%- comment -%}
        Below the kicker, not above it. With the kicker in between, «السعر
        الحالي» separated the discount from the number it describes; directly
        above the price the two read as one statement.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="pdp-save" data-savepct{% unless pdp_on_sale %} hidden{% endunless %}>{% if pdp_on_sale %}&minus;{{ pdp_pct }}%{% endif %}</span>
      <div class="pdp-prices">
        <span class="pdp-price" data-price>{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price | money }}</span>
      {%- comment -%}
        NEW-RETAIL REFERENCE. Not compare_at_price and must never become it:
        compare_at means "we used to charge this" and Shopify pushes it into the
        Product schema and Merchant feed as a price reduction. A figure that was
        never our price is misrepresentation and risks the valid Merchant
        Listings. This is a sourced, present-tense fact about what the MODEL
        costs new — plain text, never struck through, never subtracted into a
        "you save X" (we cannot know what the previous owner paid).
        Renders only when lbass.retail_ref is set. Most of this catalogue is
        vintage or generically titled, where no defensible RRP exists — blank is
        the correct outcome there, not a gap to fill with an estimate.
        Set BOTH: lbass.retail_ref (MAD digits) + lbass.retail_ref_src (source +
        original currency). The source is shown to the customer: if you cannot
        name one, do not set the price.
      {%- endcomment -%}
        {% comment %}
          Only render a genuine Shopify compare-at value; this theme never
          fabricates one.

          The percentage comes from snippets/lbass-sale, NOT from a local
          `divided_by`. Liquid floors integer division, so the old inline
          version could print a whole point below the collection card, which
          rounds half-up: on a 300 -> 193 markdown, 35% here against 36% there.
          Two numbers for one price is the failure this centralisation exists to
          prevent. The empty spans are the variant-switch targets — see the
          size-button handler, which keeps all four in step.
        {% endcomment %}
        {% comment %}
          Re-declared locally although templates/product.liquid:170 already
          assigns the same thing. This block is 550 lines below that, and it is
          the one fragment of this template that gets executed on its own by
          test/render/test_pdp_price.rb. Depending on a distant assignment made
          the block silently render an EMPTY price with no strikethrough when
          lifted out — which is also what it would do if that line above ever
          moved. Idempotent, identical, and it makes the block self-contained.
        {% endcomment %}
        {% assign selv = product.selected_or_first_available_variant %}
        {% assign on_sale = false %}
        {% if selv.compare_at_price and selv.compare_at_price > selv.price %}{% assign on_sale = true %}{% endif %}
        {% capture pct %}{% render 'lbass-sale', product: product, variant: selv %}{% endcapture %}
        {% assign pct = pct | strip %}
        {% assign diff = selv.compare_at_price | minus: selv.price %}
        <span class="pdp-old" data-old{% unless on_sale %} hidden{% endunless %}>{% if on_sale %}{{ selv.compare_at_price | money }}{% endif %}</span>
      </div>
      {%- comment -%}
        The monetary saving. The percentage answers "how good is this deal", the
        dirham figure answers "how much do I keep", and shoppers do not convert
        one into the other in their heads. Rendered outside .pdp-prices so it
        follows the page's RTL flow while the amount itself stays LTR.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="pdp-saved" data-saved dir="auto"{% unless on_sale %} hidden{% endunless %}>{{ settings.promo_save_label | default: 'وفّر' }} <span dir="ltr" data-savesum>{% if on_sale %}{{ diff | money }}{% endif %}</span></p>
      {%- if product.metafields.lbass.retail_ref != blank -%}
      <span class="pdp-retail">
        <span class="pdp-retail-m">ثمنو جديد كيسوا ~{{ product.metafields.lbass.retail_ref }} درهم</span>
        {%- if product.metafields.lbass.retail_ref_src != blank -%}
        <span class="pdp-retail-s">حسب {{ product.metafields.lbass.retail_ref_src }} · تقريبي</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Campaign announcement. Sits AFTER the retail reference on purpose, so the
        page reads: what you pay -> what it costs new -> what the campaign adds.
        Renders nothing unless snippets/lbass-promo says this piece is in the
        campaign, and it never touches the price above it — the offer discounts the
        SECOND item in the basket, which is why the badge always carries its object
        («-30% على الثانية», never a bare «-30%»). The NEW-RETAIL REFERENCE rule
        above stands unchanged: no fabricated compare-at, here or anywhere.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The stylesheet moved out of layout/theme.liquid (it is card CSS and was
        loading on cart, blog and every content page). The PDP block needs it
        too, so this template renders it here — once, immediately before the
        only element on this page that uses it.

        Ordering still holds: lbass-stamp is rendered in <head> by the layout
        and this is in the body, so the --lb-* tokens are defined and the source
        order this sheet relies on is guaranteed.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% render 'lbass-promo-css' %}
      {% render 'lbass-promo-badge', product: product, format: 'pdp' %}
      <p class="pdp-ship-line">🚚 التوصيل: <b>20 درهم داخل مراكش</b> (اختار «التوصيل المحلي» فالشيكاوت) · <b>40 درهم خارج مراكش</b> · مجاني من 500 درهم</p>
      {% comment %}
        ═══ PAYMENT CHOICE (2026-08-10) ═══
        Frames PayPal as the flexible option WITHOUT downgrading COD, which is
        the dominant and trusted method here.

        EVERY CLAIM IS TAKEN FROM /pages/refund-policy — nothing is inferred:
          • PayPal → 14 days from delivery to request a return
          • item must be unworn, unwashed, tags and packaging intact
          • RETURN SHIPPING IS PAID BY THE CUSTOMER unless the fault is ours
          • COD → inspect at the door; refuse and pay nothing; final once accepted

        The return-cost line is deliberately included. Promoting a return window
        while staying silent on who pays for it is misleading by omission, and
        the brief bans "free return" claims that are not true. It is stated
        plainly rather than buried.

        COD is NOT described as worse — the door inspection is a genuine
        protection (no money leaves before you have seen the piece), and for
        many Moroccan buyers it is the stronger guarantee. Both options are
        given equal visual weight; only the *reason* to pick each differs.

        If the policy ever changes, change /pages/refund-policy FIRST and then
        this block. The link below is the source of truth.
      {% endcomment %}
      <div class="pdp-pay" aria-label="طرق الخلاص">
        <p class="pdp-pay-h">PayPal كيعطيك مرونة أكثر</p>
        <p class="pdp-pay-b">إلا خلصتي بـ <b>PayPal</b>، تقدر تطلب الإرجاع خلال <b>14 يوم</b> من وقت ما توصلك القطعة إلا ما عجباتكش — بشرط تبقى بنفس الحالة اللي وصلاتك، مالبوساش ومامغسولاش وبالإتيكيتات. <span class="pdp-pay-note">تكاليف الإرجاع على الزبون، إلا كان الغلط من عندنا.</span></p>
        <p class="pdp-pay-b">وباقي تقدر تختار <b>الدفع عند الاستلام</b>: كتشوف القطعة فالباب قبل ما تخلص، وإلا ما عجباتكش ما تخلصش وما تاخدهاش. ملي كتخلص وكتاخدها، البيعة كتسالى.</p>
        <a class="pdp-pay-link" href="/pages/refund-policy">شوف شروط الإرجاع كاملة ←</a>
      </div>
      <p class="pdp-price-helper"><strong>هاد السعر هو السعر النهائي قبل التوصيل.</strong>{% if promo_visible %} السعر كيبقى نفسه فالسلة وما كاين حتى تخفيض مخبّي فالخلاص.{% endif %}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="pdp-condition-card" aria-label="شفافية الحالة والتوفر">
      {% if condition_confirmed %}<div class="pdp-mini pdp-condition-message"><b>{{ condition_label }}</b><span>{{ condition_description }}</span></div>{% endif %}
      {% if ticket_confirmed %}<div class="pdp-mini"><b>التّيكيت</b><span>{% if ticket_status == 'ticket_attached' %}التّيكيت الأصلي باقي متعلق{% elsif ticket_status == 'ticket_included' %}التّيكيت الأصلي داخل مع القطعة{% else %}ما فيهاش التّيكيت الأصلي{% endif %}</span></div>{% endif %}
